The $0.003 test

I would add this test to finalbuildideas.

A capability is a strong micro-payment candidate if it satisfies at least 3 of these:

Fresh — answer changes over time.

External — answer cannot be generated from the prompt alone.

Annoying — reproducing it requires several operations/integrations.

Deterministic — it can return a clean machine decision.

Expensive to be wrong — mistakes create retries, money loss, outages or bad actions.

Low-frequency per agent — not worth implementing locally.

Composable — result feeds directly into another automated action.

Normalizable — many providers/sources can be hidden behind one schema.

Evidence-producing — you can prove why the result was returned.

Data-generating — every call improves a historical dataset.

7+ = fantastic.

4–6 = useful TinyTool.

0–3 = probably a library, not a paid service.

